  "label": "intended audience",
  "description": "The target community is individuals who hold or are susceptible to Islamophobic beliefs, particularly those who may be influenced by stereotypes associating Islam with terrorism, incompatibility with Western values, or Sharia law fearmongering. The meme is designed to appeal to people who perceive Muslims as an external threat and who are motivated by divisive rhetoric to unite across racial lines against this perceived threat. The visual of clasped hands, typically a symbol of unity, is used ironically to suggest that the audience should unite against Islam, thereby targeting those who are receptive to this hateful framing.",
